    <briefdescription>
<para>Unified search across text, image, and arbitrary-embedding modalities. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="classthemis_1_1_multi_modal_search" kindref="compound">MultiModalSearch</ref> accepts a list of <computeroutput><ref refid="structthemis_1_1_modal_query" kindref="compound">ModalQuery</ref></computeroutput> components, executes each query against the appropriate backend (fulltext index for TEXT modality, VectorIndexManager for embedding modalities), and fuses the per-modality result lists using Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF).</para>
<para>This design keeps the module independent of any specific embedding model: callers are responsible for generating the embeddings (e.g. via a CLIP or Whisper model) and supplying the resulting float vectors.</para>
<para><heading level="3">Usage</heading>
</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Text<sp/>+<sp/>image<sp/>query</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">MultiModalSearch::Config<sp/>cfg;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">cfg.k<sp/>=<sp/>10;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="classthemis_1_1_multi_modal_search_1a404bb11fbc688170d9ee8d11261e7281" kindref="member">MultiModalSearch</ref><sp/>mms(&amp;sec_index,<sp/>&amp;vec_index,<sp/>cfg);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">std::vector&lt;ModalQuery&gt;<sp/>queries<sp/>=<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>{<sp/><ref refid="namespacethemis_1a8b5c83169730b83ecc8747d7800ba517a61a96ffcb251bb9bf0abf8fec19d0ea8" kindref="member">Modality::TEXT</ref>,<sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;sunset<sp/>beach&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>{},<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;text_ns&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/><sp/>0.6<sp/>},</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>{<sp/><ref refid="namespacethemis_1a8b5c83169730b83ecc8747d7800ba517a23a12f67f614b5518c7f1c2465bf95e3" kindref="member">Modality::IMAGE</ref>,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>clip_vec,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;image_ns&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>1.0<sp/>},</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">};</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>results<sp/>=<sp/>mms.search(queries);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>Thread Safety: A single <ref refid="classthemis_1_1_multi_modal_search" kindref="compound">MultiModalSearch</ref> instance is NOT thread-safe. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Exception Safety: <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacethemis_1_1search" kindref="compound">search()</ref></computeroutput> never throws; errors are returned as an empty result list. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
